[{"headword": "יוֹסֵי", "parent_lexicon": "Jastrow Dictionary", "rid": "J00217", "refs": ["Bava Batra 133b", "Pirkei Avot 2:12", "Chagigah 14b:5", "Chagigah 14b:6", "Chagigah 14b:7", "Bava Kamma 70a:16", "Eruvin 46b:4", "Eruvin 46b:6", "Eruvin 46b:7", "Eruvin 46b:8", "Eruvin 46b:9", "Zevachim 57a:7", "Tosefta Mikvaot 7:1", "Tosefta Mikvaot 8:11", "Menachot 70b:12", "Menachot 70b:15", "Sanhedrin 56a:1", "Bereishit Rabbah 65:13", "Bereishit Rabbah 65:17", "Bereishit Rabbah 65:22", "Yalkut Shimoni on Torah 115:12", "Jerusalem Talmud Eruvin 1:8:4", "Jerusalem Talmud Shekalim 7:2:3"], "content": {"senses": [{"definition": " (abbrev. of Joseph, interch. with <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_יוֹסֵף.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, יוֹסֵף 1\">יוֹסֵף</a>, <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_יוֹסָא.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, יוֹסָא 1\">יוֹסָא</a>, <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_יוֹסָא.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, יוֹסָא 1\">יוֹסָה</a>, <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_יַסָּא.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, יַסָּא 1\">יַסָּא</a>, <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_יַסָּה.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, יַסָּה 1\">יַסָּה</a>, <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_אַסִּי.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, אַסִּי 1\">אַסִּי</a>, <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_אִיסִי.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, אִיסִי 1\">אִיסִי</a>) <i>José</i> "}, {"definition": " name of several Tannaim, esp. J. b. Joezer, and J. b. Johanan. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Pirkei_Avot.1.4\" data-ref=\"Pirkei Avot 1:4\">Ab. I, 4</a>, sq. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Mishnah_Eduyot.8.4\" data-ref=\"Mishnah Eduyot 8:4\">Eduy. VIII, 4</a>; a. fr.—<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bava_Batra.133b\" data-ref=\"Bava Batra 133b\">B. Bath. 133ᵇ</a> <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_יוֹסֵף.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, יוֹסֵף 1\">יוסף</a> (Ms. H. a. R. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_יוֹסֵי.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, יוֹסֵי 1\">יוסי</a>).—R. J. hak-Kohen, or only R. J. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Pirkei_Avot.2.8\" data-ref=\"Pirkei Avot 2:8\">Ab. II, 8</a>; <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Pirkei_Avot.2.12\" data-ref=\"Pirkei Avot 2:12\">12</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Chagigah.14b.7\" data-ref=\"Chagigah 14b:7\">Ḥag. 14ᵇ</a>; Y. ib. II, 77ᵃ bot. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_יוֹסֵף.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, יוֹסֵף 1\">יוסף</a>; a. v. fr.—R. J. b. Ḥalafta, or only R. J. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bava_Kamma.70a.16\" data-ref=\"Bava Kamma 70a:16\">B. Kam. 70ᵃ</a>; <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Tosefta_Bava_Batra.2.10\" data-ref=\"Tosefta Bava Batra 2:10\">Tosef. B. Bath. II, 10</a> (v. Fr. Darkhé, p. 132). <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Eruvin.46b.9\" data-ref=\"Eruvin 46b:9\">Erub. 46ᵇ</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Mishnah_Maaser_Sheni.4.7\" data-ref=\"Mishnah Maaser Sheni 4:7\">Maas. Sh. IV, 7</a>; a. v. fr. (v. Fr. ib. p. 164, sq.).—R. J., the Galilean. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Zevachim.57a.7\" data-ref=\"Zevachim 57a:7\">Zeb. 57ᵃ</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Mishnah_Avodah_Zarah.3.5\" data-ref=\"Mishnah Avodah Zarah 3:5\">Ab. Zar. III, 5</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Tosefta_Mikvaot.7.1\" data-ref=\"Tosefta Mikvaot 7:1\">Tosef. Mikv. VII</a> (<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Tosefta_Mikvaot.8.11\" data-ref=\"Tosefta Mikvaot 8:11\">VIII), 11</a>; a. fr. (v. Fr. ib., p. 125).", "number": "1)"}, {"definition": " name of several Amoraim, esp. R. J. (in Babli <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_אַסִּי.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, אַסִּי 1\">אַסִּי</a>, in Y. also <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_יַסָּא.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, יַסָּא 1\">יַסָּא</a>, <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_יוֹסָא.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, יוֹסָא 1\">יוֹסָה</a>). Y. Ber. II, 5ᶜ bot. Y. Kil. IX, 29ᵇ bot.; <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"Jerusalem_Talmud_Eruvin.1.8.4\" data-ref=\"Jerusalem Talmud Eruvin 1:8:4\">Y. Erub. I, 19ᶜ</a>; a. v. fr.—R. J. bar Zabda, mate of R. Jonah. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"Jerusalem_Talmud_Shekalim.7.2.3\" data-ref=\"Jerusalem Talmud Shekalim 7:2:3\">Y. Shek. VII, 50ᶜ</a> bot. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Menachot.70b.15\" data-ref=\"Menachot 70b:15\">Men. 70ᵇ</a>; a. v. fr.", "number": "—2)"}, {"definition": " <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_יוֹסֵי.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, יוֹסֵי 1\">יוסי</a> or <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_יוֹסָא.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, יוֹסָא 1\">יוסה</a> a disguise of one of the Divine Names. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Mishnah_Sanhedrin.7.5\" data-ref=\"Mishnah Sanhedrin 7:5\">Snh. VII, 5</a> (<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Sanhedrin.56a.1\" data-ref=\"Sanhedrin 56a:1\">56ᵃ</a>) <span dir=\"rtl\">בכל יום … יכה י׳ את י׳</span> (v. Rabb. D. S. a. l. note) during the proceedings against the blasphemer the witnesses are requested to make their statements in disguise (v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_כִּינּוּי.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, כִּינּוּי 1\">כִּינּוּי</a>), e.g.: “the defendant said, ‘May J. strike J.’  ” (meaning, I curse Jehovah Elohim, J. Zebaoth &c.; cmp. ib. <span dir=\"rtl\">עד שיברך שם בשם</span>).", "number": "—3)"}, {"definition": " one <i>J.</i> <i> M’shitha</i>, a repentant Hellenist. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bereishit_Rabbah.65.22\" data-ref=\"Bereishit Rabbah 65:22\">Gen. R. s. 65</a> (some ed. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_יוֹסֵף.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, יוֹסֵף 1\">יוסף</a>); <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Yalkut_Shimoni_on_Torah.115.12\" data-ref=\"Yalkut Shimoni on Torah 115:12\">Yalk. ib. 115</a>.", "number": "—4)"}], "morphology": "pr. n. m."}, "plural_form": [], "alt_headwords": [], "quotes": [], "prev_hw": "יוסטתה", "next_hw": "יוֹסִינָא", "parent_lexicon_details": {"name": "Jastrow Dictionary", "language": "heb.talmudic", "to_language": "eng", "text_categories": [], "source": "Jastrow Dictionary", "attribution": "Rabbi Marcus Jastrow", "index_title": "Jastrow", "version_titl